            <div xml:id="d634">

                <pb facs="0566" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00B/10–2149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-21T16:00:00+08:00">October 21, 1949—4
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 22—3:54 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1800. Re Deptel 718, October 17, Department listing CCP Politburo 12 names Mao
                    through Kang Sheng accurate except Peng Te-huai. Wang Chia-hsiang, Chen Shao-yu,
                    Chang Wen-tien also known Politburo members. Status Peng Te-huai, Li Fu-chun, Li
                    Wei-han, Wu Liang-ping unclear. Mao is chairman Politburo, Liu Shao-chi vice
                    chairman, Chang Wen-tien secretary-general.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1800; Department pass Shanghai 1085.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
